# What Vercel leaves out of a deployment (docs/07-deployment.md §5). Deployments are built from GitHub, and
# there Vercel applies this file from the REPOSITORY root, not from this folder: an allow-list beginning with
# `/*` removed the whole repository, .git included, and the build failed. So this is a deny-list, every pattern
# is unanchored, and none may match .git or what the container build needs (app/pom.xml, app/src, media/,
# Dockerfile.vercel, .dockerignore, vercel.json). The image itself is limited further by .dockerignore.
docs/
e2e/
tools/
db/init/
BLAST/
.claude/
app/target/
.tmp/
*.md
*.ps1
docker-compose.yml
.env*
